Raw number of ascensions within a given time period is not entirely a
measure of skill either; amount of playing time is also a factor.  I
don't know how many hours a day Marvin or others can devote to playing
Nethack, but if I quit my job and life during November and played the
game for 10 hours a day I could probably rack up a pretty high amount
of ascensions as well.
 
Maybe an even better determinant of skill is % of games ascended? 
although the problem with that is that the element of luck is a lot
higher, because sometimes you just can't defend against falling on
that sleeping gas trap or running into a wand-carrying gnome...  As
far as I can tell, success with conducts is probably the closest
measure of "skill" until the ascension high score is reworked in some
way.

